@startuml
title find_me_in_wood — mesh relay: A(far, LoRa) — B(bridge: LoRa node + Bluetooth) — C(near, Bluetooth)
autonumber
participant "A\nfar member" as A
participant "B\nbridge" as B
participant "C\nnear member" as C

note over A, C : one network "hunt-2026"; edges:\nA<->B = LoRa (nodes), B<->C = Bluetooth

== A broadcasts its position ==
A -> A : GNSS fix -> beacon\n{netId, senderId=IdA, seq=41,\nttl=3, AEAD(trafficKey)}
A ->> B : LoRa (via nodes, byte pipe)

== B receives, verifies, relays ==
B -> B : AEAD opens (member ok)\nseen-cache: (IdA,41) new -> track PeerState(A)
B -> B : relay check: ttl 3>0, split horizon\n(never resend on ingress LoRa edge)
B ->> C : Bluetooth: same frame,\nttl=2, AEAD intact (B cannot and\nneed not decrypt to relay —\nbut as member it can read)

== C receives ==
C -> C : AEAD opens, seen-cache new\nPeerState(A) via relay
note over C : UI: "A · via B (LoRa)"\nstaleness per FR-6.3

== Loop / duplicate safety ==
B ->> C : (someone else re-forwards\n(IdA,41) over another edge)
C -> C : seen-cache hit -> silently dropped
A ->> B : (IdA,41) again after TTL expiry path
B -> B : seen-cache hit -> dropped
note over A, C : ttl=0 frames are never forwarded\nbeacons are periodic -> loss self-heals\non next seq
@enduml
